{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1925846,"ns":0,"title":"Brouwer–Heyting–Kolmogorov interpretation","extract":"In mathematical logic, the Brouwer–Heyting–Kolmogorov interpretation, or BHK interpretation, is an explanation of the meaning of proof in intuitionistic logic, proposed by L. E. J. Brouwer and Arend Heyting, and independently by Andrey Kolmogorov. It is also sometimes called the realizability interpretation, because of the connection with the realizability theory of Stephen Kleene.","description":"Interpretation of intuitionistic logic","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}